		<section name="node">
			<attribute key="id" type="int">50</attribute>
			<attribute key="label" type="String">There are various things to be implemented.
a. Taking input as an integer (steps 1 and 2)
b. Creating new variables (steps 1 and 2)
c. Compare two values (steps 3 and 5.1)
d. Take different actions based on a condition (steps 3, 4, 5, 5.1)
e. Displaying output (step 5.2)
f. Repeat a set of steps for a given number of times (step 5.2)

We have discussed all of the above in previous assignments multiple times. Take a paper and write the code for our algorithm.</attribute>
			<section name="graphics">
				<attribute key="x" type="double">1037.0924603174603</attribute>
				<attribute key="y" type="double">7170.113619738916</attribute>
				<attribute key="w" type="double">339.55747452503306</attribute>
				<attribute key="h" type="double">230.03436219622233</attribute>
				<attribute key="type" type="String">rectangle</attribute>
				<attribute key="raisedBorder" type="boolean">false</attribute>
				<attribute key="fill" type="String">#FFCC00</attribute>
				<attribute key="outline" type="String">#000000</attribute>
			</section>
			<section name="LabelGraphics">
				<attribute key="text" type="String">There are various things to be implemented.
a. Taking input as an integer (steps 1 and 2)
b. Creating new variables (steps 1 and 2)
c. Compare two values (steps 3 and 5.1)
d. Take different actions based on a condition (steps 3, 4, 5, 5.1)
e. Displaying output (step 5.2)
f. Repeat a set of steps for a given number of times (step 5.2)

We have discussed all of the above in previous assignments multiple times. Take a paper and write the code for our algorithm.</attribute>
